Looking at the visible dark cubes: a vertical column of three at the front‑right, plus one cube behind the bottom of that column. The two remaining cubes of the dark piece must be hidden in the back‑bottom layer, and the only connected placement that fits is a row of three cubes along the back bottom edge joined to the column.

This gives exactly the shape shown in option C: a column of three cubes with a row of three cubes attached at the bottom but shifted one layer back (a twisted L). The other options either are planar (A, B, D), have a branching cube (E), or cannot fit the visible dark faces.

\boxed{C}
